documents.question:
Consider a face-centred cubic lattice of side a. Deduce –

- (i) The primitive translation vectors;
- (ii) The volume of the primitive cell;
- (iii) The reciprocal primitive translation vectors;
- (iv) The volume of the reciprocal lattice

The volume between two concentric conducting spherical surfaces of radii a and b (a < b) is filled with an inhomogeneous dielectric with  $\epsilon = \epsilon_0/(1+cr)$ , where c is a constant and r is the radial coordinate. A charge +Q is placed on the inner surface, while the outer surface is grounded. Determine-

- (a)  $\hat{D}$  in the region a < r < b;
- (b) capacitance of the device;
- (c) polarization charge density in the region a < r < b;
- (d) surface polarization charge densities at r = a and r = b.

Determine the number of degrees of freedom for a rigid body-

- (i) moving freely in space of three dimensions;
- (ii) having one point fixed;
- (iii) having two points fixed.

Determine the discrete energy levels and the corresponding eigenfunctions for a particle in an infinitely deep potential well inside a cube of dimension L. i.e., assume

$$V(x, y, z) = 0$$
 for  $0 < x < L$ ;  
 $0 < y < L$ ;  
 $0 < z < L = \infty$  elsewhere
